# LLM Experiment Pipeline

> **Academic disclosure:** This repository contains the experimental code I developed for my thesis at University of West Florifa, currently in progress (Information Technology). It is my own original work and is shared here as a portfolio piece. The thesis title and a link will be added once finalized.

## Overview

This project is an end-to-end pipeline for running controlled experiments on large language models. Given a prompt template and a set of variables, it:

1. Generates prompts from the template
2. Queries a model with each prompt, repeatedly
3. Saves every response to a CSV file
4. Labels and summarizes the responses for analysis

The goal is to make experiments repeatable: changing an experiment means editing a template and a few settings, not rewriting code.

